  "slug": "trees-phylogenetic-d93f",
  "summary": "Three preprints supply benchmarking resources and a faster relatedness method, enabling systematic comparison of genomic inference tools at scale.",
  "synthesis": "The items share an emphasis on evaluation and computational efficiency for genomic inference, though they address different problems and none is a tree inference method itself. LRCBench compares 35 reference-free lossless compressors across 16 Oxford Nanopore and PacBio datasets on ratio, runtime, memory and robustness. OrthoSimulator generates empirically calibrated simulated datasets with known orthogroups and gene trees, giving ground truth for benchmarking orthology inference, which is closest to the phylogenetic theme. fastpmr is a memory-efficient pairwise mismatch-rate method for relatedness inference that runs over 1000x faster than READv2 and is applied to screen the global ancient DNA record. What is new is the pairing of scalable tools with explicit comparison or ground-truth frameworks, rather than a shared algorithm.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-21"
}
